---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout current="/" description="Richard J. Allen is an operations and customer-success leader with experience in SaaS support, process improvement, training, reporting, team leadership, and cross-functional execution.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Operations · Customer Success · Process Improvement · People Leadership</div>
    <h1>Helping people, processes, customers, and operations work better together.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Richard Allen, an operations and customer-success leader based in Oregon. My background combines SaaS/software support, customer experience, team leadership and coaching, process improvement, project coordination, operational reporting, training, supply operations, and change support. I’m strongest in work where teams need structure, performance needs to be measurable, and complex operations need to become clearer and more repeatable.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/case-studies/">View selected work</a><a class="button secondary" href="/resume/">View résumé</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Career impact at a glance</div><h2>Work that turns complexity into something usable.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Selected examples from operations, reporting, SaaS support, and process-improvement work.</p></div>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">100+</span></div><div class="metric-label">SOPs encompassed by a multi-month standardization initiative at Oregon Employment Department</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">workforce position records managed across multiple Oregon Health Authority divisions</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
      <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">6 yrs</span></div><div class="metric-label">in HawkSoft customer and technical support, including leadership, training, escalations, migrations, and release support</div></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>Where I add value</h2>
    <div class="grid two value-grid">
      <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">01</div><h3>Operations & people leadership</h3><p>Team leadership and coaching, workflow coverage, quality review, escalations, onboarding, reporting, and cross-functional coordination. Earlier warehouse-management experience adds supply, inventory, driver, and mixed-workforce leadership.</p><a href="/operations-leadership/">Operations & leadership →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">02</div><h3>Customer success & SaaS support</h3><p>Customer relationships, technical support, escalations, training, software adoption, database migrations, customer-journey work, release support, and customer-experience improvement.</p><a href="/customer-success/">Customer success experience →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">03</div><h3>Process improvement & documentation</h3><p>Led and revamped a multi-month SOP initiative encompassing 100+ procedures, alongside process documentation, auditing, training, reporting, and continuous-improvement work.</p><a href="/process-improvement/">Process improvement work →</a></article>
      <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">04</div><h3>Implementation & enablement</h3><p>Customer migrations, major software-release support, advance communication, launch coverage, training, onboarding, procedure development, and practical coordination between technical and customer-facing teams.</p><a href="/implementation-enablement/">Implementation & enablement →</a></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section project-work-home"><div class="container">
    <div class="project-teaser">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow light">Also available for selected project work</div>
        <h2>Need an important process documented clearly?</h2>
        <p>I take on selected short-term projects involving SOP development, workflow documentation, training guides, existing-procedure cleanup, and customer-support documentation. This is a focused project-work lane alongside my primary search for the right long-term role.</p>
        <div class="service-chips"><span>SOPs</span><span>Workflow documentation</span><span>Training guides</span><span>Process cleanup</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="/contact/">Discuss a project</a><a class="text-link-light" href="/process-improvement/">See documentation services →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="callout"><strong>Leadership beyond the workplace.</strong> Volunteer hospital chaplaincy, community administration, and service work have reinforced the same habits I value professionally: listening, organizing, mentoring, communicating clearly, and helping people through difficult situations. <a href="/community-leadership/">See community & volunteer leadership →</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
